with those words Sudan's military junta  came to an end and a transitional  sovereign council took its place  the council has five members from the  coalition known as the forces of freedom  and change and five from the military an  eleventh member agreed upon by both  sides makes up the body that will lead  Sudan's three-year transitional period  on the streets people reacted everyone  is happy and satisfied but if anything  happens and if we did not see anything  new from the revolution being achieved  we will surely hold another revolution  and topple the council same as we did  with Omar al-bashir all the members of  the sovereign council are accepted by us  the formation of the sovereign council  comes after a power-sharing agreement  was signed between the coalition and the  military on Saturday after months of  protests it had been a point of  contention between the two sides with  disagreements over its role and who will  have a bigger say now the council will  be led by the military for the first 21  months of the transitional period and by  a civilian from the forces of freedom  and change Coalition for the remaining  18 months it will have the role of  overseeing the Executive Council and  Legislative Assembly in which the  opposition will have a majority  representation the forces of freedom and  change has been representing the protest  movement and the talks to form a  transitional government and all its  institutions now people on the streets  say they'll be keeping an eye on that  coalition and the institutions including  an independent judiciary to make sure  that their demands for justice and  accountability and better living  conditions are met the weight now is for  the next steps in the journey to a  democratic rule I think one of the  interesting things here is that we are  largely expecting a fairly technocratic  cabinet to be announced during the  transitional period and the political  parties themselves will take their place  within the Legislative Council which  will be formed after 90 days so while  there might be some you know positioning  that happens within the next three years  I'm certain there will be within both  the military figures and the figures  within the executive it is in some part  offset by the structure of the  transitional government  the sovereign council is said to be a  test in the power sharing agreement  between the military and civilians  soudanese say if at the end of its  period the military does hand power to a  civilian government that's when they  will know that they're on the right  track to democracy  Hiba morgan al-jazeera cartoon  [Music]
 

